## What it covers
- The difference between reacting (a reflex) and responding (a choice).
- The pause: building a gap between what you feel and what you do.
- Why your oldest triggers fire, and how to disarm them before they run the show.
- Why being right so rarely brings peace.
- Choosing silence without suppressing yourself.
- Stepping out of the online outrage machine without going numb.
- What to do after you react, so a slip becomes useful instead of a spiral.
- A practical Toolkit: one breath, the hour rule, a nightly two minutes, an if-then plan.

## Questions the book answers
- [FAQ]({{ site.url }}/faq/): grounded answers to questions such as how to stop overreacting to small things, how to stay calm under pressure, how to control your temper, why criticism hurts, and the difference between reacting and responding.

## Writing
- [Blog]({{ site.url }}/blog/): 200 short, standalone reflections drawn from the book, one idea each, a new one every week.
